Z||000000||Robert||07-17-2000||10:50 PM||||I would like some input on my cars temperatures problems.  Some background on my car, I have installed the low temperature fan switch and a 180 thermostat.   On a recent trip, traveling at 75 mph, the temperature was a constant 180 until the outside temperature went above 80.  The temp gauge seemed to rise as the outside temp rose.  When it was about 90 outside and my temp gauge said 220.  We went up a steep incline (The Grapevine outside of LA)  and the temp went to 235.   I slowed to 60 and turned on the heater, the temp dropped to 220.  We then got stuck in traffic, i.e. Los Angeles at 2 pm. and a strange thing happened; the temp dropped to 180.  The other Fiero’s in my group heated up in traffic, mine cooled off.  George of the Fiero Shop thinks I may need a new radiator, what do you guys think?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/fierosig.GIF">  <BR>87GT - "Thunder"||||reg||5
